Sectoral composition of gross emissions by municipal type

:::

@fig-composicao-tipo shows that land-use change and forestry is the largest sector in every type, with a share ranging from 58.4% (T5) to 68.4% (T3). T5, which includes Cuiabá, Rondonópolis and Sinop, has the highest energy share (10.1%). Emissions from agriculture and livestock differ most between types (ε² = 0.33), as the tests in @tbl-testes-tipo show.

