::: {.callout-note collapse="true" appearance="simple"}
## Emissions per family farm and per hectare of family-farm area (interpret with caution)

Article B divided municipal emissions by the number of family farms and by family-farm area. SEEG measures the entire municipality, so these ratios **do not represent the emission intensity of family farming** and serve only as context. Per family farm, they range from 1,954 tCO2e (T5) to 4,521 tCO2e (T4) per year. As @tbl-intensidades shows, the difference between types is weak per family farm (p = 0.034; ε² = 0.07) and not significant per hectare (p = 0.118).

::: {#tbl-intensidades}


