::: {.achado}
As @tbl-desmat-tipo shows, the 141 municipalities recorded a total of 22,969 km² of deforestation from 2017 to 2025, with T1 (74 municipalities) accounting for 34.5%. The types differ little, however: the difference is weak for total area deforested (Kruskal-Wallis: H = 9.68; p = 0.046; ε² = 0.07) and not significant for the percentage of territory deforested (p = 0.234).
:::

As in Article A, deforestation does not track the share of family farms in category 46504 of the 2017 Census. Across the 141 municipalities, Spearman's ρ is 0.05 (p = 0.522) with total area deforested and 0.04 (p = 0.666) with the percentage of territory deforested (@tbl-testes-desmat).

