<h4>Correction note (19 October 2026)</h4>
<ul>
<li>The PRODES series previously used in the project contained Amazon data entered by hand and labelled as the official series. In every year from 2005 to 2024, this series lay above the official rate for Mato Grosso.</li>
<li>That series was replaced by the official INPE series, retrieved from TerraBrasilis on 19 October 2026. The new series contains the annual rate for Mato Grosso in the Legal Amazon and the annual increment by biome. The website does not use the old series.</li>
<li>This replacement changes the validation in Article B. For the 2010–2020 state total, the proxy is about 8 times the PRODES figure (previously “2.6 times”). The statement about “weak interannual agreement” no longer holds, because the Pearson correlation with the official rate is 0.65.</li>
<li>The text of Article B has not yet been rewritten, but the figures in this section already use the official series.</li>
</ul>
</div>
